   "title": "Read me first",
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## 13 · RTX upscale of a finished clip\n\nTakes a clip this extension has already rendered and upscales it with NVIDIA's\nVideo Super Resolution — nothing is re-sampled, and the soundtrack is kept. No\nH3 model is needed.\n\n**Needs:** [NVIDIA RTX Nodes](https://github.com/Comfy-Org/Nvidia_RTX_Nodes_ComfyUI)\nand [VideoHelperSuite](https://github.com/Kosinkadink/ComfyUI-VideoHelperSuite),\nand an NVIDIA RTX card.\n\n**Paste a path into `VHS_LoadVideoPath`:** a take from the project folder\n(`clips/NN_name/video/vNN_….mp4`), a clip from the render cache, or the joined\nfilm.\n\n* **scale** 1.0–4.0, or switch `resize_type` to target dimensions.\n* **quality** LOW / MEDIUM / HIGH / ULTRA.\n* **fps** must match the source — every clip this extension writes is 24.\n\nAn 832×480 clip of 14 s doubled to 1664×960 in about 16 s on an RTX 4070 Ti.\nThe result lands in `output/vig_h3/`."
   ],
   "widgets_values_named": {
    "text": "## 13. RTX upscale of a finished clip\n\nTakes a clip this extension has already rendered and doubles it with NVIDIA's\nVideo Super Resolution. Nothing is re-sampled: the frames are read off the file,\nupscaled, and written back with their own soundtrack.\n\n**Paste the path into `VHS_LoadVideoPath`.** A take out of the project folder\n(`clips/NN_name/video/vNN_....mp4`), a cache clip, or the joined film -- any\nfile, since this node takes a path rather than an upload.\n\n**Measured on a real clip, 20 Sep 2026:** 832x480 -> 1664x960, 340 frames,\n14.17 s, audio kept (aac 32 kHz stereo) -- **16.2 s** for the whole thing, about\n1.1 s of work per second of film. 4.1 MB in, 10.2 MB out.\n\n### The settings\n\n* **scale** 1.0-4.0, or switch `resize_type` to *target dimensions* for exact\n  pixels. The node rounds to a multiple of 8 either way.\n* **quality** LOW / MEDIUM / HIGH / **ULTRA**. ULTRA is what the numbers above\n  were measured at; the cost of the lower ones has not been measured here.\n* **fps must match the source**, and every clip this extension writes is 24.\n  `CreateVideo` cannot read it off the file, so it is typed in.\n\n### What this is NOT\n\nA pass over the ALREADY ENCODED clip. The Cutter decodes its frames, writes the\nh264, and this reads them back -- so there is one generation of compression\nbetween the sampler and the upscaler that an upscaler inside the render graph\nwould not have. Whether that shows on this material has not been measured.\n\nNothing here touches the board, the cache or the timeline: the upscaled file\nlands in `output/vig_h3/` and is yours to use as you like."
   },
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
